Actually doing "make install" with root privileges using su is enough,
everything else in the compilation process *can* be done as a regular
user.

If you look at sys/unix/Install.unx, you may see that the only place where
it says anything about root privileges is in section 7, at line 77:

    Type 'make all' from the top directory to set up all the auxiliary
    files the main executable will use.  Then become root if necessary and
    type 'make install'.  Everything should now be set.

(Mark, are you sure this is the instruction file you read and followed?)

